        "urduTitle": "علامات و نشانیاں",
        "text": "Kidney stones often cause no pain while they are in the kidneys, but they can cause sudden, severe pain as they travel from the kidneys to the bladder. Usually pain appears at side belly or groin and the colour of urine becomes pinkish or reddish. These are common indications of kidney stones.\n\nAnyone may develop a kidney stone, but people with certain diseases and conditions or those who are taking certain medications are more susceptible to the stone development. Kidney stones form when there is a decrease in urine volume and/or an excess of stone-forming substances in the urine.\n\nKidney (cut open)",
