        "urduTitle": "انسانی عصبی نظام کے تقسیمات",
        "text": "Human nervous system is primarily divided into central nervous system (CNS) and peripheral nervous system (PNS). CNS acts as a coordinating center while PNS provides communication among receptors, CNS, and effectors. Further division of nervous system are given in the following table.\n\ninformation: initiates action)\n\n(receives and processsensory information; initiates response;\n\nstores memories; generates thoughts and emotions)\n\nSpinal Cord (conducts signals to and from brain; controls reflex activities)\n\nPeripheral Nervous System (PNS)\n\n(transmits signals between the CNS and the rest of the body)\n\nMotor neurons (carry signals from the CNS that control the activities of muscles and glands)\n\nSomatic Nervous System (controls voluntary movements by the activation of skeletal muscles)\n\nSensory neurons (carry signals to the CNS from sensory organs)\n\nAutonomic Nervous System (controls involuntary responses by influencing organs, glands and smooth muscles)\n\nSympathetic Division (prepares the body for stressful or energetic activity; \"fight or flight\")\n\nMain division of nervous system",
