        "urduTitle": "ہارمون: کیمیائی پیغام رساں",
        "text": "The glands are structures made up of one or more cells that make and release some product called secretion. These glands are classified as exocrine glands and the endocrine glands. Exocrine glands (exo = outside; crine = to secrete), secrete their products onto the target surface directly or through ducts. Liver, salivary glands, sweat glands, and the tear glands have ducts; the unicellular goblet cells on the other hand directly release mucin on the target surface by exocytosis. Endocrine glands (endo = within; crine = to secrete) are ductless glands. They produce hormones, and secrete by exocytosis directly into the extracellular spaces. From there the hormones enter the blood or lymphatic fluid and travel to specific target site.",
