        "urduTitle": "رویہ اور محرکات",
        "text": "The ability of an organism to respond against particular stimuli varies from the relatively simple action of the growth of a plant stem towards a light source, to the complex sexual behavior patterns of territory defense, courtship and mating seen in birds and mammals. In other words, what a person, animal, plant, or any organism does after being stimulated, is part of its behavior. In order to cause that response, the stimulus must be sensed, processed, and interpreted.",
