        "urduTitle": "واسا ایفرینشیا",
        "text": "About 10 to 20 vasa efferentia collect sperms from inside the testes and transfer them to the epididymis.\n\nThe epididymis rests on the backside of each testis. Most of the epididymis consists of the highly coiled duct of the epididymis with an uncoiled length of about 6 m(20 feet). Its functions are the transport and storage of the sperms. Here the sperms are stored temporarily, nourished, and they gain the ability to swim.",
