          "The anterior end of the neural tube becomes the brain and the rest becomes the spinal cord. The associated neural crest cells migrate widely and give rise to the cranial, spinal, and sympathetic ganglia (and associated nerves), to the medulla of the adrenal gland, and to pigment cells, and contribute to some connective tissues.",
          "By the end of the first month of development, the three primary brain vesicles (fore-, mid-, and hindbrain) are obvious. By the end of the second month, all brain flexures are evident; the cerebral hemispheres cover the top of the brain stem, and brain waves can be recorded. Most of the remaining ectoderm forming the surface layer of the embryonic body differentiates into the epidermis of the skin."
